v2.0.0 rebuilt the Baccarat module as a local Python server application. v2.1.0-v2.4.0 added the Tie
bet and its own stake, the half-screen layout, PASS recording the table's result, and the OCR
groundwork. v2.5.x-v2.7.x built and proved the OCR tooling, calibration, the confidence gate and the
live loop. v2.8.x connected the setup screen to the reader, added one-click and drawn calibration,
fixed the drawing coordinate bug, and pre-measured the Pragmatic half-width profile.

v2.9.0 showed the capture region live in the OCR panel and fixed the three reasons the live reader
produced nothing (pixel-identical double-read rule, an unreadable reply freezing the loop, a read gap
straddling the settle), then read BANKER from the live screen. v2.9.1 fixes the latency: a clear
reading is now accepted on one model call (~2-4s) instead of two (~5-16s), the loop interval is 0.6s,
the provider timeout is 15s, and the panel shows the measured reading time.

